208
00:12:51.812 --> 00:12:55.900
[officer 1] Here. I came around back
when we first got here

209
00:12:55.983 --> 00:13:01.030
and there's a back door that was open
with one track of footprints in the snow.

210
00:13:01.864 --> 00:13:04.950
[Anthony] The officers.
when they first went through the scene.

211
00:13:05.451 --> 00:13:08.329
the back door was ajar.
it was slightly open.

212
00:13:08.412 --> 00:13:12.875
And we knew that none of our officers
had come and gone from that door.

213
00:13:14.293 --> 00:13:17.046
[officer 5] So I got
about a size 13-and-a-half shoe here.

214
00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:21.133
coming and going.
rounds that log. goes back down that way.

215
00:13:21.217 --> 00:13:23.511
[intriguing music playing]

216
00:13:25.346 --> 00:13:28.349
No. uh…
No weapon we've been able to locate?

217
00:13:28.432 --> 00:13:31.769
We haven't moved anybody.
but I'd ascertain it's probably not here.

218
00:13:31.852 --> 00:13:33.521
-Yeah.
-[officer 2] But…

219
00:13:35.064 --> 00:13:37.900
Looks like there's some dried blood
on the sink.

220
00:13:37.983 --> 00:13:39.693
but there's not any around it.

221
00:13:43.948 --> 00:13:47.368
[Anthony] 1122 King Road
was a three-story home.

222
00:13:48.661 --> 00:13:51.705
On the third floor were two rooms.

223
00:13:52.414 --> 00:13:57.419
and the room to the right
was where we found two female victims.

224
00:13:59.129 --> 00:14:02.007
Going downstairs
to what would be the main floor.

225
00:14:02.091 --> 00:14:06.554
just at the bottom of the stairs.
was another bedroom. and that was empty.

226
00:14:07.471 --> 00:14:10.015
Off of that was the living room area.

227
00:14:10.724 --> 00:14:13.435
Off of the living room area.
down a short hallway.

228
00:14:13.519 --> 00:14:14.728
was another bedroom.

229
00:14:15.479 --> 00:14:18.816
and that is where
we found the male and female victims.

230
00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:23.779
Down at the bottom level.
so the street level. was another bedroom.

231
00:14:24.864 --> 00:14:27.575
We found traces of blood
throughout the house.

232
00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:33.622
We also found a knife sheath
in the third-floor bedroom

233
00:14:33.706 --> 00:14:35.416
laying next to one of the victims.

234
00:14:39.712 --> 00:14:43.966
We knew that was going to be
something of high importance.

235
00:14:46.176 --> 00:14:48.596
[officer 2] Who'd like a blanket?
It's temporary.

236
00:14:48.679 --> 00:14:50.097
Would anybody like one?

237
00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:51.765
For your feet? To stand on?

238
00:14:51.849 --> 00:14:53.517
-[Dylan] I'll take one.
-[officer 2] Okay.

239
00:14:53.601 --> 00:14:55.728
[Anthony] As we started talking
to people involved.

240
00:14:55.811 --> 00:14:59.148
we found out there were roommates
that were home. Dylan and Bethany.

241
00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:04.945
They were able to advise information
of who else were roommates in the home.

242
00:15:05.821 --> 00:15:08.532
-[officer 2] Who's Xana?
-[Dylan] Xana is the girl in there.

243
00:15:08.616 --> 00:15:10.868
-[officer 2] Is the girl… This one?
-[Dylan] Yeah.

244
00:15:11.535 --> 00:15:13.954
-[officer 2] Do you know how old she is?
-She's 20.

245
00:15:14.622 --> 00:15:16.790
[officer 2] The guy that lives here.
his name is what?

246
00:15:16.874 --> 00:15:19.251
-Or he's usually here. Ethan.
-[Dylan] Oh. Ethan… Chapin.

247
00:15:19.335 --> 00:15:22.171
[officer 2] And. um…
So Ethan. how old is Ethan?

248
00:15:22.254 --> 00:15:24.256
[Dylan] I believe he just turned 20.

249
00:15:24.757 --> 00:15:28.719
And then there's Maddie Mogen
and Kaylee up top.

250
00:15:29.428 --> 00:15:31.513
-[officer 2] How old is Maddie?
-[Dylan] She's 21.

251
00:15:33.015 --> 00:15:34.350
[officer 2] How old is Kaylee?

252
00:15:34.433 --> 00:15:36.602
[Dylan] Over 21. I believe she's 21 or 22.

253
00:15:36.685 --> 00:15:39.229
-Sorry. I don't fully remember.
-[officer 2] It's okay.

254
00:15:40.064 --> 00:15:42.483
-You're doing great.
-[Dylan] Thanks. I'm scared.

255
00:15:42.566 --> 00:15:44.777
[officer 2] I'm asking a lot of you.
so I appreciate…

256
00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:48.197
-[Dylan] Sorry if I don't say anything.
-[officer 2] You're doing very well.

257
00:15:48.948 --> 00:15:51.575
[Bethany] Maddie and Kaylee
came home from the club.

258
00:15:51.659 --> 00:15:54.787
[officer 2] Do you know how long
they were there? Till closing. at least?

259
00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:55.996
[Bethany] Yeah.

260
00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.456
[Dylan] I was in my room.

261
00:15:57.539 --> 00:16:00.376
And I was trying to go to bed.
and I heard Kaylee go upstairs.

262
00:16:00.459 --> 00:16:03.379
Like. "I'm gonna go to sleep now.
She's going upstairs."

263
00:16:03.462 --> 00:16:06.173
And then. all of a sudden.
I heard her scream.

264
00:16:06.256 --> 00:16:09.218
[voice wavering] And she ran downstairs
'cause she saw someone.

265
00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:12.054
That's what I'm pretty sure she said.
"Someone's here."

266
00:16:12.137 --> 00:16:14.515
And she screamed and just ran downstairs.

267
00:16:14.598 --> 00:16:17.017
I called her name.
but I jumped up and locked my door

268
00:16:17.101 --> 00:16:18.602
because I was so scared.

269
00:16:18.686 --> 00:16:21.855
And then I heard her go in…
I think it was the bathroom.

270
00:16:21.939 --> 00:16:23.399
And I remember her sobbing.

271
00:16:23.482 --> 00:16:26.235
I remember hearing this guy's voice
that I didn't recognize saying.

272
00:16:26.318 --> 00:16:30.406
"You're going to be okay. I'm gonna help."
But I don't know how to explain it.

273
00:16:30.489 --> 00:16:34.368
It wasn't in a nice way.
It was a weird way. Like. a weird tone.

274
00:16:34.451 --> 00:16:36.370
[officer 2] "You're gonna be okay."

275
00:16:36.453 --> 00:16:38.288
-"I'm gonna help you."
-[Dylan] Yeah.

276
00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:41.709
[officer 2] You didn't hear anything
from Kaylee anymore?

277
00:16:41.792 --> 00:16:43.711
[Dylan] No. after that
I didn't hear anything.

278
00:16:43.794 --> 00:16:44.837
[officer 2] Okay.

279
00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:47.631
[Dylan] So then I kept calling her name.

280
00:16:47.715 --> 00:16:50.551
On my phone.
I called Xana. Maddie. and Kaylee

281
00:16:50.634 --> 00:16:52.052
and none of them answered.

282
00:16:52.553 --> 00:16:55.973
So then I opened up the door to look
and that's when I saw the guy pass by.

283
00:16:56.056 --> 00:16:58.976
He looked at me. but he didn't
come towards me or say anything.

284
00:16:59.059 --> 00:17:02.062
Which was really confusing to me.
I don't understand that.

285
00:17:02.146 --> 00:17:05.441
I'm pretty sure he went out the side door.
I didn't know what to do.

286
00:17:05.524 --> 00:17:07.860
-[officer 2] Four this morning?
-[Dylan] 4:00 a.m.. yes.

287
00:17:07.943 --> 00:17:11.113
[mysterious music playing]

288
00:17:11.196 --> 00:17:14.575
[Anthony] Just off of the kitchen area
would have been Dylan's room.

289
00:17:15.701 --> 00:17:21.123
She said she saw a male figure
in the living room. dressed in all black.

290
00:17:22.708 --> 00:17:24.793
Their eyes met. They saw each other.

291
00:17:25.502 --> 00:17:29.548
For whatever reason. the perpetrator
continued to walk towards the kitchen.

292
00:17:29.631 --> 00:17:35.179
and Dylan shut her door and locked it
out of fear. and the perpetrator left.

293
00:17:36.513 --> 00:17:38.932
She had tried
to get a hold of her other roommates

294
00:17:39.016 --> 00:17:40.684
and she ended up getting Bethany.

295
00:17:40.768 --> 00:17:43.479
Bethany was downstairs.
in her room on the bottom floor.

296
00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.940
Bethany told her to come downstairs

297
00:17:47.024 --> 00:17:48.400
and Dylan opened her door.

298
00:17:48.484 --> 00:17:51.737
ran downstairs and spent
the rest of the night with Bethany.

299
00:17:53.614 --> 00:17:57.367
Our officers were able to find out that
Bethany and Dylan called a friend

300
00:17:57.451 --> 00:17:59.036
and a friend's boyfriend to come over

301
00:17:59.119 --> 00:18:03.540
so they could have someone come check on
the rest of the roommates.

302
00:18:04.958 --> 00:18:07.753
The boyfriend had. when he arrived.

303
00:18:07.836 --> 00:18:09.630
is the one who entered the home.

304
00:18:09.713 --> 00:18:14.093
went upstairs
and saw Xana and Ethan deceased.

305
00:18:18.847 --> 00:18:20.015
Jesus. man.

306
00:18:21.809 --> 00:18:22.851
What happened?

307
00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:27.147
[officer 5] So. uh. I did call Aaron
and I heard him checking the service.

308
00:18:27.231 --> 00:18:31.443
Just said. "Hey. these kids are gonna need
some sort of counselor to talk to."

309
00:18:31.527 --> 00:18:33.779
-Cap's got it taken care of.
-[officer 5] Cool.

310
00:18:33.862 --> 00:18:35.781
That's taken care of.

311
00:18:35.864 --> 00:18:38.450
One girl was in there.
Did you hear that part of it?

312
00:18:38.534 --> 00:18:40.869
-[officer 5] Mm-mm.
-There was another girl that was in here.

313
00:18:40.953 --> 00:18:44.706
saw a guy walk in with a ski mask on

314
00:18:46.208 --> 00:18:48.669
and. uh. locked herself in her room.

315
00:18:49.628 --> 00:18:52.756
-Heard all of this shit going on.
-[officer 5] Holy shit.

316
00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:54.466
And she didn't call last night?

317
00:18:54.967 --> 00:18:56.510
It happened at four.

318
00:18:56.593 --> 00:18:58.220
[officer 5] This girl's lucky to be alive.

319
00:18:58.303 --> 00:19:00.347
She probably didn't make a peep
and locked her door.

320
00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:02.516
Probably didn't know that she was there.

321
00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:08.856
[Anthony] We asked the question.
why did the roommates wait eight hours

322
00:19:08.939 --> 00:19:10.649
to call the police?

323
00:19:11.191 --> 00:19:14.528
There are so many reasons why you may not.

324
00:19:14.611 --> 00:19:16.697
People are in shock. it's traumatic.

325
00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:19.324
I mean. I can't imagine being of that age

326
00:19:19.408 --> 00:19:23.453
and being able to comprehend
that this horrific thing just occurred.

327
00:19:24.246 --> 00:19:27.833
-[intriguing music playing]
-[chatter over police radio]

328
00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:33.797
[Cooper] My apartment
was backed up into that King house.

329
00:19:33.881 --> 00:19:38.177
probably ten yards from the front door
of their house.

330
00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:40.429
And you could see it
right from my bedroom.

331
00:19:41.054 --> 00:19:42.055
Um…

332
00:19:43.056 --> 00:19:46.018
This is gonna be tough.
This is gonna be real tough. Um…

333
00:19:47.561 --> 00:19:49.479
I woke up. I looked out my window

334
00:19:49.563 --> 00:19:53.442
and heard a bit of what was going on.
screaming. crying and stuff.

335
00:19:53.525 --> 00:19:58.405
I saw some of the girls
sitting out there with the. with the cop.

336
00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:01.909
And so. my first thought was.

337
00:20:01.992 --> 00:20:05.120
something's wrong with.
you know. Ethan and Xana.

338
00:20:05.204 --> 00:20:08.165
My first thing was Hunter.
Ethan's brother.

339
00:20:09.416 --> 00:20:11.501
We were all in Sigma Chi together.

340
00:20:12.127 --> 00:20:14.838
And so. I went and got shoes.

341
00:20:14.922 --> 00:20:17.674
went and grabbed Hunter
from the Sigma Chi house.

342
00:20:19.509 --> 00:20:20.886
I woke him up.

343
00:20:20.969 --> 00:20:23.972
I was like. "Hey. have you heard
from Ethan or Xana?"

344
00:20:24.056 --> 00:20:27.267
He was panicking. I was like. "What are
you talking about? What's going on?"

345
00:20:27.351 --> 00:20:29.519
Tries to call him. no answer.

346
00:20:29.603 --> 00:20:33.357
Um… So we're walking over there.
and he's like. "What's going on?"

347
00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:36.693
I'm like. "I don't know.
I don't have any answers for you. I just…"

348
00:20:39.238 --> 00:20:40.948
And I saw Hunter Johnson.

349
00:20:41.531 --> 00:20:46.411
He just told Hunter Chapin
Ethan and Xana weren't there anymore.

350
00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:50.666
I mean. how do you process that. you know?

351
00:20:51.208 --> 00:20:53.210
It's hard to see everyone

352
00:20:54.378 --> 00:20:56.046
figure out what was going on.

353
00:21:00.842 --> 00:21:05.347
For some reason. in the moment. I didn't
feel like it was my place to be there.

354
00:21:06.556 --> 00:21:09.184
So I walked back up to my apartment.

355
00:21:10.227 --> 00:21:13.272
And there's my girlfriend. Addie.

356
00:21:13.355 --> 00:21:15.899
and my roommates and their girlfriends

357
00:21:15.983 --> 00:21:19.653
and told them that they're gone.

358
00:21:20.612 --> 00:21:22.614
-Um…
-[music stops]

359
00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:24.741
It's pretty hard.

360
00:21:27.119 --> 00:21:28.954
[melancholic music playing]

361
00:21:29.037 --> 00:21:31.123
[woman] Ethan. look at me. Smile!

362
00:21:31.999 --> 00:21:33.083
Say cheese.

363
00:21:35.836 --> 00:21:39.381
[Cooper] Ethan. he was one
of the most kind people

364
00:21:39.464 --> 00:21:41.425
you will ever run into in your life.

365
00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:46.430
He'd walk into a room
and the energy would light up

366
00:21:47.055 --> 00:21:49.266
and would genuinely make you smile.

367
00:21:52.561 --> 00:21:57.524
[Maya] Xana and Ethan instantly were
best friends from the very beginning.

368
00:21:58.567 --> 00:22:00.902
I could kinda tell
she was starting to like him

369
00:22:00.986 --> 00:22:04.531
because Xana and I had
a ritual every single morning.

370
00:22:04.614 --> 00:22:07.659
Because before Xana moved
into the King Street house.

371
00:22:07.743 --> 00:22:09.286
we lived next door to each other.

372
00:22:09.369 --> 00:22:12.372
I'd wake up and I would go into
Xana's room and say good morning.

373
00:22:12.456 --> 00:22:14.708
Or she'd wake up
and come and say good morning.

374
00:22:14.791 --> 00:22:16.126
just whoever woke up first.

375
00:22:16.209 --> 00:22:18.086
Then I started noticing. you know.

376
00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:21.923
Xana hasn't been coming to my room
so often in the mornings. That's weird.

377
00:22:22.007 --> 00:22:25.427
So I would go into her room
and little did I know. there's Ethan.

378
00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:29.222
And I'd be like. "Hello. Ethan.
Good morning. Good to see you."

379
00:22:29.306 --> 00:22:30.682
He really loved her.

380
00:22:32.684 --> 00:22:35.771
I mean. you could see it.
They were made for each other.

381
00:22:42.361 --> 00:22:44.529
[officer 2] I'll be right back
with you. okay?

382
00:22:46.823 --> 00:22:49.868
-[J] Hello?
-[officer 2] Hey. J. Sorry to bug ya.

383
00:22:50.369 --> 00:22:53.622
Um… we have
a quadruple homicide on campus.

384
00:22:53.705 --> 00:22:56.833
Can you come in and start.
uh… just man the street?

385
00:22:56.917 --> 00:22:59.044
-[text alert]
-[woman 1] So they can text you…

386
00:23:00.712 --> 00:23:02.631
-…so fucked up.
-[person crying]

387
00:23:02.714 --> 00:23:05.801
[woman 2] You could have told us
that happened before they sent a text.

388
00:23:05.884 --> 00:23:07.886
[officer 2] I have no idea
what you're talking about.

389
00:23:07.969 --> 00:23:10.097
[woman 2] They sent a text
to the entire university

390
00:23:10.180 --> 00:23:11.932
before even telling us what happened.

391
00:23:12.015 --> 00:23:14.851
Obviously we know.
but it'd be nice to have a confirmation.

392
00:23:16.561 --> 00:23:19.189
[Blaine] I got a call
from the Moscow Police Department.

393
00:23:19.272 --> 00:23:21.900
He said. "Blaine. we have
four dead individuals."

394
00:23:21.983 --> 00:23:25.821
"We think they may be college students."
And I was just flabbergasted.

395
00:23:25.904 --> 00:23:28.740
All kinds of questions
go through your mind.

396
00:23:28.824 --> 00:23:31.243
How? Who? Why? What happened?

397
00:23:31.326 --> 00:23:32.786
[mysterious music playing]

398
00:23:32.869 --> 00:23:36.665
The protocol for us at the institution
when we learn a crime has occurred

399
00:23:36.748 --> 00:23:41.002
is to use the Vandal Alert system
so we can get information out immediately.

400
00:23:42.295 --> 00:23:44.047
[officer 2] Hey. ma'am. Ma'am?

401
00:23:44.881 --> 00:23:47.592
Can you stop there for me?
Can you come back down here?

402
00:23:48.218 --> 00:23:50.470
We're not gonna have
anybody come back this way.

403
00:23:50.554 --> 00:23:53.890
-[woman] Gonna go to my friend's house.
-[officer 2] They up here?

404
00:23:53.974 --> 00:23:57.018
-[woman] Yeah.
-[officer 2] Let's walk on the road.

405
00:23:58.562 --> 00:24:00.480
[Anthony] It was a chaotic scene.

406
00:24:00.564 --> 00:24:03.608
There were people coming out
of all sorts of residences around.

407
00:24:03.692 --> 00:24:05.402
They knew something was going on.

408
00:24:05.485 --> 00:24:07.487
People were starting to get upset.

409
00:24:07.571 --> 00:24:10.782
[officer 2] Hey. can you guys
stay here for a little bit?

410
00:24:10.866 --> 00:24:12.993
-[man 1] Yeah.
-[officer 2] Is that okay?

411
00:24:13.076 --> 00:24:17.747
You know. it's ongoing panic.
and phone calls. texts.

412
00:24:17.831 --> 00:24:20.542
Everyone's starting to know
and freak out and…

413
00:24:20.625 --> 00:24:22.294
[mysterious music playing]

414
00:24:22.377 --> 00:24:24.254
That Vandal Alert said "homicide."

415
00:24:24.796 --> 00:24:26.423
That's a pretty heavy word.

416
00:24:27.007 --> 00:24:30.510
And most of us at that point knew
that they weren't alive anymore.

417
00:24:30.594 --> 00:24:32.429
but still didn't know what happened.

418
00:24:32.929 --> 00:24:34.264
No one had the answers.

419
00:24:34.764 --> 00:24:37.767
Everyone was talking.
saying different things.

420
00:24:39.644 --> 00:24:41.855
[man 2] Are you the one to ask
what's going on there?

421
00:24:41.938 --> 00:24:45.484
[officer 2] Yeah. I can't tell you.
though. So. um…

422
00:24:45.567 --> 00:24:47.694
Yeah. if everybody could just stay inside.

423
00:24:47.777 --> 00:24:52.282
We didn't get a heads-up
that they were going to put out the alert.

424
00:24:52.365 --> 00:24:53.617
We would have preferred

425
00:24:53.700 --> 00:24:57.454
that that information
would have been collaborated with us

426
00:24:57.537 --> 00:25:02.209
prior to it going out.
because on the scene we had four victims.

427
00:25:02.292 --> 00:25:05.670
We had to not only identify the victims.
and then start working diligently

428
00:25:05.754 --> 00:25:08.173
to get a hold of their next of kin
and notify them.

429
00:25:09.174 --> 00:25:12.469
And when the university put out the alert.

430
00:25:12.552 --> 00:25:16.264
that information started being shared
before we were able to.

431
00:25:16.348 --> 00:25:19.935
[people crying]

432
00:25:20.018 --> 00:25:22.062
[Maya] I had texted Xana

433
00:25:22.145 --> 00:25:24.523
and was like.
"Hey. did you get the Vandal Alert?"

434
00:25:24.606 --> 00:25:25.649
No response.

435
00:25:25.732 --> 00:25:29.528
Checked her location. She was at home.
So I was like. "That's weird."

436
00:25:29.611 --> 00:25:32.572
Immediately. the sororities
and fraternities did head counts.

437
00:25:32.656 --> 00:25:35.700
so they account for everyone
who's in the house.

438
00:25:35.784 --> 00:25:37.452
Whether you live in or you don't.

439
00:25:37.536 --> 00:25:40.914
they make sure that
all of their people are accounted for.

440
00:25:41.915 --> 00:25:47.128
That's how I kind of found out that
Xana and Maddie weren't accounted for.

441
00:25:47.879 --> 00:25:50.674
[melancholic music playing]

442
00:25:51.800 --> 00:25:56.054
Throughout my whole time at Moscow
there haven't been too many Vandal Alerts.

443
00:25:56.137 --> 00:25:58.932
Nothing ever that bad happens here.

444
00:25:59.015 --> 00:26:01.977
We all watch over each other.
have each other's backs.

445
00:26:03.228 --> 00:26:06.064
Xana and I had Finance class together.

446
00:26:06.147 --> 00:26:10.110
She was kind of freaking out
'cause she needed to get an A on this test

447
00:26:10.193 --> 00:26:12.988
in order to get a good grade
in the class and stuff like that.

448
00:26:13.071 --> 00:26:18.743
so. she was asking me if we could go
to the library tutoring sessions

449
00:26:18.827 --> 00:26:20.161
on that Sunday.

450
00:26:21.162 --> 00:26:23.957
And then when we got that Vandal Alert

451
00:26:24.040 --> 00:26:26.585
I was texting her and calling her.

452
00:26:26.668 --> 00:26:28.128
Couldn't get through to her.

453
00:26:28.211 --> 00:26:31.381
So then I got in contact
with her sister. Jazzmin.

454
00:26:33.300 --> 00:26:35.468
[Jazzmin] Xana's my little sister.

455
00:26:36.553 --> 00:26:38.972
Growing up. it was just my dad and us.

456
00:26:40.265 --> 00:26:42.976
Once I went to college.

457
00:26:43.059 --> 00:26:44.227
we got really close.

458
00:26:44.311 --> 00:26:48.356
and then she went to college like.
you know. ten minutes away from me.

459
00:26:50.191 --> 00:26:53.612
[Jeff] Jazzmin was
seven miles away at WSU.

460
00:26:54.154 --> 00:26:55.905
so they could see each other.

461
00:26:56.364 --> 00:27:00.493
Knowing that they were close to each other
was a little more comforting.

462
00:27:01.036 --> 00:27:03.705
[contemplative music playing]

463
00:27:03.788 --> 00:27:06.708
[Jazzmin] The weekend
of November 12th and 13th.

464
00:27:06.791 --> 00:27:10.629
we had the Wazzu football game on Saturday

465
00:27:10.712 --> 00:27:13.923
that my dad and I went to
with a bunch of our friends.

466
00:27:15.300 --> 00:27:17.719
He wanted Xana and Ethan to come too.

467
00:27:17.802 --> 00:27:20.930
but they really wanted to go
to the University of Idaho football game.

468
00:27:21.848 --> 00:27:24.225
I was pushing for it. them to come over.

469
00:27:25.101 --> 00:27:27.312
but they didn't make it
over there that night.

470
00:27:28.313 --> 00:27:31.441
The next day. my dad left.

471
00:27:31.524 --> 00:27:34.653
and he was gonna go check on Xana

472
00:27:34.736 --> 00:27:37.113
because she needed
a light fixed in her car.

473
00:27:38.531 --> 00:27:40.617
[Jeff] I was gonna stop by Xana's.

474
00:27:40.700 --> 00:27:42.786
I called and she didn't answer. and I go.

475
00:27:42.869 --> 00:27:45.622
"You know what?
She's probably sleeping in."

476
00:27:45.705 --> 00:27:50.377
It was a cloudy day.
Really bad day was what it was.

477
00:27:50.460 --> 00:27:52.045
[tense music playing]

478
00:27:52.128 --> 00:27:55.632
So I just started driving out of town.
and I got about ten miles out.

479
00:27:55.715 --> 00:27:59.094
and Jazzmin had got a call
from a couple of Xana's friends.

480
00:27:59.177 --> 00:28:02.222
"Hey Jazz. I'm not exactly sure
if you've heard what's going on.

481
00:28:02.305 --> 00:28:05.183
but there's something
that happened on King Street."

482
00:28:05.266 --> 00:28:06.976
Started calling Xana and Ethan.

483
00:28:07.602 --> 00:28:11.064
and I started calling
some of Xana's best friends and…

484
00:28:11.856 --> 00:28:15.026
I called my dad and I told him
that he should probably turn around

485
00:28:15.110 --> 00:28:17.487
because something bad happened.

486
00:28:18.238 --> 00:28:20.407
[Jeff] I just stopped the car.

487
00:28:21.408 --> 00:28:23.660
So I raced back down there. and…

488
00:28:23.743 --> 00:28:25.036
[chatter over police radio]

489
00:28:25.120 --> 00:28:28.415
They had the crime tape
100. 200 feet off the house

490
00:28:28.498 --> 00:28:30.041
so it rounded the whole thing.

491
00:28:30.125 --> 00:28:33.002
They wouldn't let nobody
within that distance of it.

492
00:28:35.380 --> 00:28:37.632
[Jazzmin] There's no ambulances.
there's nothing.

493
00:28:37.716 --> 00:28:40.051
so. I didn't know what to believe.

494
00:28:41.052 --> 00:28:43.888
I just asked if I could go see my sister.

495
00:28:43.972 --> 00:28:47.058
They just didn't say anything.
and I didn't know what was going on.

496
00:28:48.685 --> 00:28:53.565
I was approached by a male. and he said.
"My daughter lives in that house."

497
00:28:53.648 --> 00:28:58.570
They told me that we needed to go
to the police station. They wanted to…

498
00:28:59.571 --> 00:29:00.780
to talk to us.

499
00:29:00.864 --> 00:29:03.742
[melancholic music playing]

500
00:29:10.290 --> 00:29:14.836
[Anthony] I've done. unfortunately.
many death notifications in my career…

501
00:29:17.422 --> 00:29:21.551
but that's definitely got to be
one of the hardest I've ever had to do.

502
00:29:26.014 --> 00:29:28.475
[Jazzmin] We were just confused.
We were shocked.

503
00:29:28.558 --> 00:29:31.811
We didn't know what happened at all.

504
00:29:33.521 --> 00:29:36.649
But I had all this adrenaline.
and I think my dad the same.

505
00:29:36.733 --> 00:29:40.028
We just. we didn't know.
What do you do in that situation?

506
00:29:40.111 --> 00:29:43.281
Like. no one knows.
So that was really. really hard.

507
00:29:46.868 --> 00:29:49.537
I just left after that. They told me.

508
00:29:50.038 --> 00:29:52.916
"There's nothing you can do.
You can't see anything or d…"

509
00:29:52.999 --> 00:29:54.751
There's nothing I could do.

510
00:29:54.834 --> 00:29:57.754
It was the best thing I could do.
I couldn't deal with it.

511
00:29:59.297 --> 00:30:00.298
You know?

512
00:30:07.180 --> 00:30:08.556
[Kristi] November 13th.

513
00:30:09.057 --> 00:30:11.142
You know. it was a normal day.

514
00:30:13.019 --> 00:30:15.480
I got a phone call from my niece. Sabrina.

515
00:30:16.397 --> 00:30:18.066
She was hysterical.

516
00:30:18.775 --> 00:30:22.862
She told me that she thought
something bad had happened to Kaylee.

517
00:30:22.946 --> 00:30:25.031
[melancholic music continues]

518
00:30:26.449 --> 00:30:29.828
[voice wavering] And she said.
"Aunt Kristi. I think Kaylee's dead."

519
00:30:32.997 --> 00:30:35.500
Her husband's cousin lives down there.

520
00:30:35.583 --> 00:30:37.710
and he said there was a party.

521
00:30:37.794 --> 00:30:40.046
and somebody went in
and shot up the party.

522
00:30:40.129 --> 00:30:41.589
and Kaylee got shot.

523
00:30:41.673 --> 00:30:45.051
I tried Kaylee first.
Her phone went straight to voicemail.

524
00:30:45.927 --> 00:30:47.887
And then I called her sister. Alivea.

525
00:30:49.472 --> 00:30:51.391
[tense music playing]

526
00:30:51.474 --> 00:30:57.564
[Alivea] I had two or three missed calls
from my mom and a missed call from my dad.

527
00:30:57.647 --> 00:31:01.734
That's always kind of a red alert.
you know. something's happening.

528
00:31:01.818 --> 00:31:03.486
So I call her back.

529
00:31:03.570 --> 00:31:05.321
I could hear the panic in her voice.

530
00:31:05.405 --> 00:31:09.325
I say. "Okay. I'll start calling around.
I'll talk to you in a few."

531
00:31:11.244 --> 00:31:14.122
I reach out to some of the roommates

532
00:31:14.205 --> 00:31:16.040
that Kaylee had in the house.

533
00:31:16.124 --> 00:31:17.667
And I reached out on Instagram.

534
00:31:17.750 --> 00:31:21.504
Basically just said. "Hey.
heard that maybe an accident happened."

535
00:31:21.588 --> 00:31:24.173
"Can you just have Kaylee
get a hold of us?"

536
00:31:24.757 --> 00:31:28.887
And. of course. in between this.
I'm calling Kaylee. I'm calling Maddie.

537
00:31:28.970 --> 00:31:34.058
I'm not getting through.
but it's not really alarming to me yet.

538
00:31:35.602 --> 00:31:38.980
[Kristi] I started calling Maddie.
Her phone would just ring and ring.

539
00:31:39.522 --> 00:31:41.900
I'm still not understanding
why Maddie's not answering.

540
00:31:42.692 --> 00:31:44.819
I called Maddie's mom. Karen.

541
00:31:44.903 --> 00:31:47.655
and I said. "Have you heard
about something is going on?"

542
00:31:47.739 --> 00:31:50.366
She said. "We're on it.
Scott and I are driving down."

543
00:31:50.450 --> 00:31:53.995
"We're 25 minutes away from Moscow."

544
00:31:54.078 --> 00:31:56.497
"We're going to pick up the girls.
They're fine."

545
00:31:56.581 --> 00:31:58.082
"We're picking up the girls."

546
00:31:58.166 --> 00:32:00.168
I knew in my heart

547
00:32:01.377 --> 00:32:02.921
that they weren't fine.

548
00:32:03.421 --> 00:32:06.132
And I was like. "Okay. Karen. Okay."

549
00:32:06.215 --> 00:32:08.718
[melancholic music playing]

550
00:32:10.511 --> 00:32:13.556
[Steve] When your child has a relationship
with somebody else

551
00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:16.351
and gets to that point
of a true best friend.

552
00:32:16.893 --> 00:32:20.396
your families kind of blend together. and…

553
00:32:21.189 --> 00:32:23.191
-[Kaylee] Say hi. Maddie.
-Hi.

554
00:32:23.274 --> 00:32:25.151
[Steve] She had that with Maddie.

555
00:32:25.234 --> 00:32:27.862
It's just me and Maddie
out here by the pool.

556
00:32:29.822 --> 00:32:31.866
Soaking up the sunshine.

557
00:32:35.536 --> 00:32:39.040
[Kristi] I started getting messages
in my Facebook saying.

558
00:32:39.123 --> 00:32:41.960
"I'm so sorry for your loss."
"I'm so sorry for your loss."

559
00:32:42.043 --> 00:32:44.170
"I'm so sorry for your loss."
And I'm like.

560
00:32:45.254 --> 00:32:50.134
"No. no. no. no! This can't be real.
you know?" And. uh…

561
00:32:51.010 --> 00:32:52.887
And that sheriff pulled up.

562
00:32:53.554 --> 00:32:57.100
I'd actually took off
running to the bedroom because I knew.

563
00:33:05.024 --> 00:33:09.237
[Steve] The officer just tells us that
not only our daughter has passed away.

564
00:33:09.320 --> 00:33:11.739
but Maddie has passed away as well.

565
00:33:12.573 --> 00:33:16.828
And I'd just gotten off the phone
with Karen. Maddie's mother. and Scotty.

566
00:33:16.911 --> 00:33:20.540
and we knew that they were
probably ten. 15 minutes away

567
00:33:20.623 --> 00:33:22.333
from showing up on site.

568
00:33:22.417 --> 00:33:25.169
They're in Moscow.
and from what I've been told.

569
00:33:25.253 --> 00:33:27.213
they were told at the police department.

570
00:33:32.802 --> 00:33:36.347
[Anthony] Every human being
reacts differently.

571
00:33:36.431 --> 00:33:37.974
or uniquely. to grief.

572
00:33:39.767 --> 00:33:44.397
I've given death notifications where
I've had individuals almost strike me.

573
00:33:45.023 --> 00:33:47.608
I've had others
that they were inconsolable.

574
00:33:48.609 --> 00:33:52.697
And none of the reactions are…
There's no wrong reaction.

575
00:33:52.780 --> 00:33:54.157
I'm a father as well.

576
00:33:54.240 --> 00:34:00.371
And I could not imagine
what they. not only went through.

577
00:34:00.455 --> 00:34:03.541
but continue to go through
with the loss of their children.

578
00:34:04.250 --> 00:34:06.085
[music fades]

579
00:34:06.169 --> 00:34:08.546
[officer 6] We're gonna do
a neighborhood canvass.

580
00:34:08.629 --> 00:34:12.091
So. I need to know
who's available here to start with me.

581
00:34:12.175 --> 00:34:14.177
-[indistinct chatter]
-[officer 7] I can.

582
00:34:14.260 --> 00:34:16.179
[moody dramatic music playing]

583
00:34:16.262 --> 00:34:21.184
[Anthony] Information in any investigation
is important to keep close to the vest.

584
00:34:21.267 --> 00:34:22.351
[knocking]

585
00:34:22.435 --> 00:34:25.688
As much as we would like to share
information in investigations

586
00:34:25.772 --> 00:34:28.858
so that people were informed.
it puts everyone at risk.

587
00:34:29.442 --> 00:34:32.820
[officer 2] Did you guys hear anything.
see anything last night or this morning?

588
00:34:32.904 --> 00:34:34.447
[woman] Can you tell us what happened?

589
00:34:34.530 --> 00:34:36.741
[officer 2] We can't tell you
what's going on right now.

590
00:34:36.824 --> 00:34:40.578
Also. we can't have the offender.
the perpetrator.

591
00:34:40.661 --> 00:34:42.413
knowing what information we have.

592
00:34:42.497 --> 00:34:46.751
They could use that
to further disappear or do it again.

593
00:34:47.418 --> 00:34:50.463
-[officer 2] Hello. Huh?
-[man 1] What's going on? What's going on?

594
00:34:50.546 --> 00:34:52.381
-[officer 2] I can't tell you.
-[man 1] Really?

595
00:34:52.465 --> 00:34:53.633
[officer 3] Yeah. Sorry.

596
00:34:53.716 --> 00:34:57.762
In order to keep the case pure
and whole and untainted.

597
00:34:58.513 --> 00:35:01.015
we need to preserve
the integrity of the case.

598
00:35:02.016 --> 00:35:05.478
[man 2] Yeah. I didn't hear anything
last night. I was home all night.

599
00:35:05.978 --> 00:35:07.897
Nothing out of the ordinary for me.

600
00:35:07.980 --> 00:35:10.399
With this case. we relied on our partners

601
00:35:10.483 --> 00:35:13.236
with the Idaho State Police
and their forensics folks.

602
00:35:14.028 --> 00:35:16.823
They were in that house
looking for everything.

603
00:35:16.906 --> 00:35:18.991
And it took hours and hours.

604
00:35:20.952 --> 00:35:22.453
As far as evidence we collected.

605
00:35:22.537 --> 00:35:26.082
the knife sheath
was obviously a big portion.

606
00:35:26.165 --> 00:35:29.710
We wanted to make sure that
that got forensically analyzed

607
00:35:29.794 --> 00:35:31.295
as quickly as possible.

608
00:35:31.379 --> 00:35:33.548
[moody dramatic music fades]

609
00:35:34.799 --> 00:35:38.136
[Jack] Can I… Can I ask
what's going on? [indistinct]

610
00:35:38.219 --> 00:35:40.096
[officer 2] Where are you living at?

611
00:35:40.179 --> 00:35:44.267
[Jack] I live right over there.
but that's my ex-girlfriend of five years.

612
00:35:44.350 --> 00:35:46.936
[officer 2] Trying to figure out
what's going on? Okay.

613
00:35:47.019 --> 00:35:50.940
I'll have you sit here for a second.
We'll have someone talk with you. okay?

614
00:35:51.691 --> 00:35:53.693
Do you wanna sit in the car for a second?

615
00:35:53.776 --> 00:35:57.989
Just so we can keep you separated
from the people that were. uh. around.

616
00:35:58.072 --> 00:35:59.907
[Jack] Trying to find out what's going on.

617
00:35:59.991 --> 00:36:02.368
[officer 2] I'll have someone
talk to you. okay?

618
00:36:02.451 --> 00:36:03.703
I appreciate it. Thanks.

619
00:36:05.913 --> 00:36:09.584
Guy just walked up to me and said.
"Can I talk to you? What's going on?"

620
00:36:09.667 --> 00:36:13.921
He said… I said. "Oh. Who are you?
Do you live here or something?"

621
00:36:14.005 --> 00:36:18.759
He says. "No. that's my ex-girlfriend
of five years that's in there."

622
00:36:18.843 --> 00:36:21.596
"I don't know what's going on.
I live right over here."

623
00:36:21.679 --> 00:36:23.848
[tense music playing]

624
00:36:25.016 --> 00:36:26.434
[Baylie] Jack is my cousin.

625
00:36:26.934 --> 00:36:29.896
Jack started dating Kaylee
sophomore year of high school.

626
00:36:29.979 --> 00:36:33.399
They went to the same high school.
and ended up going to the same college.

627
00:36:34.358 --> 00:36:36.444
She was graduating soon.

628
00:36:37.111 --> 00:36:42.366
and she had just landed a pretty big job
in Austin. Texas. actually.

629
00:36:43.618 --> 00:36:46.245
I was surprised.
She's been here her whole life.

630
00:36:46.746 --> 00:36:49.165
But I knew. I mean.
she was very spontaneous.

631
00:36:49.248 --> 00:36:51.250
And I was like. "Oh. that makes sense."

632
00:36:52.293 --> 00:36:55.004
I think Kaylee
and Jack were on a break at this time.

633
00:36:55.087 --> 00:36:58.090
She kinda just was like.
"I'm just. you know. going with life

634
00:36:58.174 --> 00:37:02.053
and try to adventure
by myself for a little."

635
00:37:03.429 --> 00:37:09.477
On that day.
I was at my mom's store in Hayden. Idaho.

636
00:37:09.560 --> 00:37:15.691
and I got a call from my good friend
at University of Idaho.

637
00:37:15.775 --> 00:37:18.986
She said. "I think Kaylee passed away."

638
00:37:19.820 --> 00:37:23.366
And I think
I kinda went into a state of denial.

639
00:37:23.449 --> 00:37:25.201
I was kind of like.

640
00:37:25.868 --> 00:37:28.996
"What do you mean? Um. like Kaylee who?"

641
00:37:29.080 --> 00:37:31.582
And I just. I couldn't get myself to

642
00:37:32.416 --> 00:37:35.086
grasp the fact that it could be my Kaylee.

643
00:37:37.213 --> 00:37:39.715
I was trying to call Jack's sister.

644
00:37:39.799 --> 00:37:41.842
She was bawling when I answered the phone.

645
00:37:42.843 --> 00:37:47.056
She said that Jack was
in the back of a cop car.

646
00:37:48.140 --> 00:37:50.518
[Jack] I wanted to speak to someone
about what's going on.

647
00:37:50.601 --> 00:37:53.479
[officer 2] Give me just a second.
I understand your dog's upstairs?

648
00:37:53.562 --> 00:37:56.565
[Jack] I'm not worried about my dog.
I'm worried about what happened.

649
00:37:56.649 --> 00:37:57.942
I don't know anything.

650
00:38:00.152 --> 00:38:02.446
Got a guy here
that's the ex of one of them.

651
00:38:02.530 --> 00:38:05.491
-He's detained in this car at the moment.
-[officer 5] Yeah.

652
00:38:06.075 --> 00:38:07.076
[officer 2] Okay.

653
00:38:07.785 --> 00:38:10.746
[Anthony] It's typical
in a case of this nature

654
00:38:10.830 --> 00:38:13.958
for the ex-boyfriend
to be a person of interest.

655
00:38:14.041 --> 00:38:17.420
and so it was very important
for us to talk with him.

656
00:38:18.170 --> 00:38:22.174
-[Jack] I just wanna know what's going on.
-[officer 2] Get with you in a minute.

657
00:38:25.344 --> 00:38:29.390
[Anthony] Someone who kills somebody
with a knife. it's very personal.

658
00:38:30.641 --> 00:38:34.061
There were theories about
was it some relationship gone bad?

659
00:38:34.145 --> 00:38:36.314
Was it a fellow student?

660
00:38:37.106 --> 00:38:39.734
We didn't know if it was
somebody that they knew or not.

661
00:38:39.817 --> 00:38:42.611
so many people were brought back
to the Police Department.

662
00:38:42.695 --> 00:38:44.739
and our detectives were going one by one.

663
00:38:44.822 --> 00:38:46.741
having interviews with each one of them.

664
00:38:47.908 --> 00:38:50.161
That included Jack DuCoeur.

665
00:38:50.244 --> 00:38:53.205
who we learned
was the ex-boyfriend of Kaylee.

666
00:38:53.289 --> 00:38:54.623
[tense music continues]

667
00:38:54.707 --> 00:38:58.502
At this point. I felt so helpless.
I'm over a thousand miles away.

668
00:38:59.045 --> 00:39:00.713
What can I do?

669
00:39:00.796 --> 00:39:04.216
And then I get a text
from my sister Autumn.

670
00:39:04.842 --> 00:39:07.303
and she said. "The cops are here."

671
00:39:08.346 --> 00:39:09.764
"She's dead. Alivea."

672
00:39:12.350 --> 00:39:14.977
And I just said. "Okay. I'm on my way."

673
00:39:15.686 --> 00:39:19.357
I basically just needed to get there
as fast as possible.

674
00:39:21.192 --> 00:39:24.195
My husband's driving.
My kids are sleeping in the back here.

675
00:39:24.820 --> 00:39:27.323
At this point. I'm not crying. I'm okay.

676
00:39:27.406 --> 00:39:29.617
And then that's when
I start thinking to myself.

677
00:39:30.743 --> 00:39:33.996
if something happened last night.
they're gonna call someone.

678
00:39:34.997 --> 00:39:39.085
Kaylee's phone
was on my parents' little plan.

679
00:39:40.044 --> 00:39:43.089
I asked my mom to give me the password
so that I could log into it.

680
00:39:44.465 --> 00:39:47.051
I got into the account.

681
00:39:47.134 --> 00:39:51.263
Kaylee had not called 911 at any point.

682
00:39:51.347 --> 00:39:54.517
but I did notice that she had called Jack

683
00:39:54.600 --> 00:39:56.435
quite a few times.

684
00:39:57.770 --> 00:40:01.482
The calls first started
some time around 2:00 a.m.

685
00:40:01.565 --> 00:40:05.778
They eventually ended
some time around 3:00 a.m.

686
00:40:07.488 --> 00:40:11.575
I'm thinking it wasn't out of the ordinary
for Kaylee to do that.

687
00:40:12.159 --> 00:40:14.620
But. of course.
that's something that looks odd

688
00:40:14.703 --> 00:40:16.372
when you know what has happened.

689
00:40:18.124 --> 00:40:20.626
[detective] We're trying to collect
as much information as we can

690
00:40:20.709 --> 00:40:22.378
to get a picture on what's going on

